      vignette:'A 6-year-old girl is brought to the emergency department by her parents after they found her unresponsive in the basement.  They report that her younger sister sprayed the patient with a bottle that had been filled with pesticide to help rid the house of insects.  Temperature is 36.6 C (98 F), blood pressure is 110/60 mm Hg, pulse is 58/min, and respirations are 42/min.  On examination, the patient is lethargic and salivating.',
      q:'Which of the following medications should be administered first during treatment of this patient\'s current condition?',
